+## Session lifecycle error path
+
+A throw from `beforeSession` takes the same path through the lifecycle as any other failure in the turn: `onError` sees it, `afterSession` still runs, and the rejection reaches the caller unchanged. Because `afterSession` then runs for a session whose turn never started, a cleanup hook cannot tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished": it must tolerate being handed the session with nothing past `beforeSession` done — no user input read, no model response produced.
+
+- `onError` fires for a throw from `beforeSession` with the same argument shape as any other orchestrator failure — the session and the thrown `Error` — and the original rejection still reaches the caller unchanged ([validated by: runs onError and still rejects with the same error when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- `afterSession` fires after `onError` for that throw and receives the same session, so a deployer that allocates in `beforeSession` and releases in `afterSession` sees the release run even when the allocation itself failed ([validated by: runs afterSession after onError when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
